In summary, this listens to an ALSA PCM capture interface and automatically
records a memory buffer if the learned magnitude of the target frequency drops
or picks up again.

The code is in a bit of a rough shape, don't expect too much out of it.

REQUIREMENTS:
- DUB
- A D compiler (dmd, gdc, or ldc2)
- libasound2-dev (ALSA dev library)

